  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Grace, you're verified. I found the order and the restaurant has no open incidents. Your order had a $15 FALL15 promo, so here are the options for each missing item.\n\n**Grain bowl ($18.00)**\n- **Refund:** $13.50 to your Visa ending 4242, plus $4.50 in account credit. The $4.50 is the bowl's share of the promo discount.\n- **Credit:** $21.60 in account credit (the price plus 20%).\n\n**Lemonade ($4.00, one of the two)**\n- **Refund:** $3.00 to your Visa, plus $1.00 in account credit for its share of the promo.\n- **Credit:** $4.80 in account credit.\n\nThere is a $25 limit on account credit per conversation. Taking both items as credit would total $26.40, which is over the limit. If you choose credit for both, I'd have to refund one of them to your card instead.\n\nWhich would you like for each item, refund or credit?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for laying that out. I order from Green Bowl a lot, so I'd rather have the grain bowl as account credit. For the lemonade, I'd like the money back on my card. Does that split work?"
  },
